---
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What Merkleye collects, what it deliberately never receives, and why a self-hosted product changes that answer."
  updated="[EFFECTIVE DATE]"
>
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      Merkleye runs on your infrastructure. Your monitored domains, the
      certificates it observes, and every finding it produces stay on your
      machines and are never transmitted to us. That is an architectural
      property of the product, not a promise about our intentions.
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <p>
    The controller of any personal data described here is
    <span class="tbd">[ENTITY LEGAL NAME]</span>,
    <span class="tbd">[REGISTERED ADDRESS]</span>. Contact
    <a href="mailto:privacy@merkleye.com">privacy@merkleye.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What we never receive</h2>
  <p>
    Because the software is self-hosted, we do not receive, and have no means
    of obtaining:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>the domains you monitor, in any form, including hashed;</li>
    <li>
      certificates, subject alternative names, issuers, serials, or
      fingerprints observed by your deployment;
    </li>
    <li>findings, risk scores, alerts, or notification contents;</li>
    <li>your configuration file, database, API tokens, or webhook URLs;</li>
    <li>
      the addresses or hostnames of any infrastructure your deployment watches
      or runs on.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    On hashing specifically: we do not accept hashed domain names either. The
    set of registrable domains is small enough to enumerate, so a hash of a
    domain can be reversed by brute force and is not anonymous. Treating it as
    though it were is a common industry error and we do not rely on it.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we do collect</h2>

  <h3>Website</h3>
  <p>
    This site is static and ships effectively no JavaScript. It sets
    <strong>no cookies</strong>. Your light/dark preference is stored in your
    browser&rsquo;s <code>localStorage</code>, never transmitted, and readable
    only by this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our host, <span class="tbd">[Cloudflare Pages]</span>, processes standard
    server logs (IP address, user agent, requested path, timestamp) to serve and
    protect the site. We use <span class="tbd">[no analytics / a
    cookieless, non-identifying analytics product]</span>.
  </p>

  <h3>Trial requests and enquiries</h3>
  <p>
    If you request an evaluation licence or contact us, we collect the name,
    work email address, and organisation you provide, and the correspondence
    itself. We use it to issue your licence file, to answer you, and to follow
    up about the evaluation.
  </p>

  <h3>Customers</h3>
  <p>
    For paid licences we hold billing contact details, the licence records we
    issue, and payment metadata. Card details go to our payment processor and
    are never held by us.
  </p>

  <h3>Support diagnostics — off by default</h3>
  <p>
    Merkleye can optionally send a small daily operational summary — version,
    platform, counts, plugin health, error-class counters — to help us diagnose
    problems for customers on a support plan. It is
    <strong>disabled by default</strong>, opt-in by explicit configuration, and
    has a local-only mode that writes the same payload to disk so an
    air-gapped deployment can attach it to a ticket without any network egress.
    It never contains domain names, certificates, findings, or configuration.
    You can print the exact payload before enabling it. The full proposal and
    the complete never-send list are published in the repository.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Legal bases</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Basis (UK/EU GDPR)</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Server logs</td>
        <td>Serving and securing the site</td>
        <td>Legitimate interests</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Trial and enquiry details</td>
        <td>Issuing licences, replying, evaluation follow-up</td>
        <td>Steps prior to a contract; legitimate interests</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Customer and billing records</td>
        <td>Performing the licence agreement; tax and accounting</td>
        <td>Contract; legal obligation</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Support diagnostics</td>
        <td>Providing contracted support</td>
        <td>Contract (and opt-in)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>4. Retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Server logs: <span class="tbd">[30]</span> days.</li>
    <li>
      Trial and enquiry records: <span class="tbd">[24]</span> months from last
      contact.
    </li>
    <li>
      Customer and billing records: the term plus
      <span class="tbd">[7]</span> years, as tax law requires.
    </li>
    <li>Support diagnostics: 13 months.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We share personal data only with the subprocessors listed on the
    <a href="/legal/subprocessors/">Subprocessors</a> page, and where required
    by law. <strong>We do not sell personal data, and we do not share it for
    advertising or cross-context behavioural advertising.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    We are established in <span class="tbd">[JURISDICTION]</span>. Where data
    leaves the UK/EEA it is transferred under the UK IDTA or the EU Standard
    Contractual Clauses, as set out in the
    <a href="/legal/dpa/">Data Processing Addendum</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct,
    delete, port, or restrict processing of your personal data, to object to
    processing based on legitimate interests, and to withdraw consent. Under
    the CCPA/CPRA you may also request disclosure of the categories collected
    and opt out of sale or sharing — neither of which we do.
  </p>
  <p>
    Write to <a href="mailto:privacy@merkleye.com">privacy@merkleye.com</a>. We
    respond within 30 days. If you are in the UK or EEA and unsatisfied, you
    may complain to your supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    Material changes are announced on this page with a new effective date, and
    emailed to customers with an active licence.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
